X:10
T: Hounds of Bedlam
T: Tune: Mad Maudlin's Search for Tom O'Bedlam
M: 4/4
K: C
"Verse" A/A/ | Aaga e2 d c/d/ | eged ee z A | Aaga ee d c/d/ | eged ee z2 | 
| "Chorus" ee d c/B/ c2 c/B/ A | B2 A A/B/ cd ee | z cd ee d cB | c2 BA B2 cd | eA BG AA z |
W:
W: For to see my Tom of Bedlam, ten thousand miles I'll travel
W: Mad Maudlin goes on dirty toes, for to keep her shoes from gravel
W: 
W: Chorus:
W: Still I sing bonny boys, bonny mad boys
W: Bedlam boys are bonny
W: For they all go bare and they live by the air
W: And they want no drink nor money
W: 
W: No shih tzu, pug, nor dachshund shall keep my Mad Tom from me
W: I'll howl all night, the stars I'll bite, the fray shall well become me.
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: I went down to Satan's kitchen for to get me food one morning
W: And there I saw souls piping hot, all on a spit a-turning
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: And when that I have murdered the Man in the Moon to a powder
W: His staff I'll break, his dog I'll shake. There'll howl no demon louder
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: My staff has murdered giants, my bag a long knife carries
W: For to cut mince pies from children's thighs, with which to feed the fairies
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: So let's drink to Tom of Bedlam, he'll fill the sea in barrels
W: We'll drink it all, well brewed with gall. With Mad Maudlin I will travel.
W: 

