X:12
T:I Can Hew
T:Tune: Collier Lads
H:Source: Bassett Street Hounds
C:David Dodds
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:Am
%
AB c2 A2 | ee e<e d2 | cd e>e ee | dc AG A2 |
w: I can hew, boys, I can hack it out; I can hew the coal,_ I can dance and shout. 
%
AB c2 A2 | ee e<e d2 | cd ee ee | dc  AG A2 |]
w: I can hew, boys, coal that's black and fine; I'm a col- lier lad_ work- in' down the mine.
W:
W: 1. On Saint Monday's Day it's well I do admire
W: To be sittin' at home, by me own coal fire
W: Then it's down to the pub, for a glass or two 
W: For to work on a Monday, that would never do.
W: 
W: 
W: 2. Well I likes my whiskey and I likes my beer
W: I’ll drink 14 pints and I’ll not feel queer
W: I can hold my whiskey good as any man
W: And I’ll dance and sing as long as I can
W:
W:
W: 3. Well my boy is 14, he's a strapping lad,
W: And he'll go to the pit soon, just like his dad.
W: Then when Friday comes, we'll pick up our pay,
W: And we'll drink together to round out the day.
W:
W: 
W: 4. And it’s when I’m dead, oh I know full well
W: I’ll not go to heaven, I am bound for hell
W: And my pick and shovel, old Nick he will admire
W: Then he’ll set me to hewing for his own hellfire

