X:15
T: Lost In Boston
T: Tune: Charlie on the MTA
T: Lyrics: The Team that Always Returns
H: Lyrics by Susan Galbraith, Laura Waterstripe, Dan Clark
H: Dance by the Bassett Street Hounds
M: 4/4
K: F
ff | ff ff fF2 F | B2 Bc df ed | cf2 f g2 f2 | e4-e a2 g | 
ff ff fF FF | B2 B2 df ed | cf2 f ag ag | f4-f "Chorus:"fg_a | aaaa2 g2 f | 
gf ff2-f fg | a2 a2 agf2 | g4-g z fg | a2 a-a2 gfd | f2 f g2 f fg | 
a3 f ede2 | f4-f z:| "Tag:"c d c _e4-e | 
W:
W: Oh, we often come to Boston, to dance with our friends there
W: But the driving can make us scream
W: When a lack of road signs mixes with some botched directions
W: It all feels like a fever dream
W: 
W: (Chorus:)
W: But do we ever return? Yes, we always return
W: So I guess we'll never learn.
W: Though we're lost forever on the streets of Boston
W: We're the team that always returns.
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: We expected trouble, so we thought we'd ask a native,
W: And we got her to draw a map.
W: First she sent us to a rotary, we went three-fourths 'round it
W: And we fell in a Moebius trap.
W: 
W: Chorus
W: 
W: When we called our native guide and said we're getting nowhere,
W: Can you help us to find the Pike?
W: She said "I thought that I had given you the right directions,
W: But I go everywhere by bike."
W: 
W: Chorus
W:
W: When we called our other teammates on their handy cell phones to say
W:"Sorry, we're running late," 
W: Tom said "My GPS has sent us to a cemetery.
W:Hope that you can avoid our fate."
W: 
W:Chorus
W: 
W:We keep turning at the corner with the Dunkin' Donuts 
W: And the gas station on the right,
W:But every signless road leads to the same damn rotary
W: And now you understand our plight.
W:
W: Chorus
W:
W: Tag: Or never left

